                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_03\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit removes the properties `OUTPUT_ENCODING` (\"html.outputEncoding\") and `SOURCE_ENCODING` (\"html.sourceEncoding\") from IReportProperties.java, along with their getters/setters (getOutputEncoding/setOutputEncoding, getSourceEncoding/setSourceEncoding) in ReportProperties.java, and restores/adds the properly-named `OUT_ENCODING` (\"out.encoding\") and new `IN_ENCODING` (\"in.encoding\") properties with getOutEncoding()/getInEncoding(). It also updates all call sites in the html/txt/xml report generators back to use getOutEncoding()/getInEncoding() instead of getOutputEncoding()/getSourceEncoding().\n\nCandidate_01 (the initial project import) only contains the original, correct scheme: IReportProperties.OUT_ENCODING = \"out.encoding\" and ReportProperties.getOutEncoding()/setOutEncoding(), used consistently by all report generators, with plain FileReader (no explicit source encoding) for reading source files. There is no OUTPUT_ENCODING/SOURCE_ENCODING at this point.\n\nCandidate_03 is the commit that introduces the bug: it adds `OUTPUT_ENCODING = \"html.outputEncoding\"` and `SOURCE_ENCODING = \"html.sourceEncoding\"` to IReportProperties.java (explicitly commented \"// addition parameters by terry\"), removes the previously working getOutEncoding()/setOutEncoding() methods entirely, adds getOutputEncoding()/setOutputEncoding() and getSourceEncoding()/setSourceEncoding(), and changes the property-parsing code to read from the new (non-standard) \"html.outputEncoding\" key instead of the documented \"out.encoding\" key. It also rewires all call sites (html/txt/xml ReportGenerator.java) to call getOutputEncoding() instead of getOutEncoding(), and changes source file reading to use getSourceEncoding(). This silently changes/breaks the user-facing property name for controlling output encoding (from \"out.encoding\" to \"html.outputEncoding\"), which is exactly the regression that the fix commit reverts.\n\nCandidate_04 is an unrelated, small change (renaming NESTED_ITEMS_PARENT_DIRNAME from \"_files\" to \"files\") and does not touch the encoding properties at all, so it did not introduce or worsen the bug.\n\nCandidate_05's diff is textually identical to the fix commit's diff (same blob hash transition 907d9c1 -> 87e6bf4 for IReportProperties.java), meaning it represents the same fix already being applied earlier in this candidate ordering (likely a duplicate/cherry-pick recorded in history) \u2014 it is a fix, not the bug introduction.\n\nSince candidate_03 is the first and only candidate that introduces the problematic OUTPUT_ENCODING/SOURCE_ENCODING property scheme that the fix commit removes, it is the bug-introducing commit.\n"
                }
